00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:38.790
But Starcraft wasn't the only game that saw

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:42.869
gambling create controversy around the
scene. A large portion of the money that

00:10:42.869 --> 00:10:46.290
came in with the influx of new investors
in 2016,

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:50.339
particularly in CS:GO, was coming from
websites that allowed counter-strike

00:10:50.339 --> 00:10:52.460
players to wager their in-game items.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:57.220
Yesterday and the day before, I have amassed probably an amount of about $16,000.00

00:10:57.220 --> 00:11:00.760
and if you don't believe me, let me just show you part of
my inventory.

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:01.980
They sponsored the game's

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:05.640
most popular players, the biggest
tournaments and everything else.

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:09.100
and we found this new site called CS:GO Lotto.

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:11.600
Though largely unregulated, these websites

00:11:11.609 --> 00:11:16.379
appeared to be relatively harmless on the
surface. That was until a youtuber called

00:11:16.379 --> 00:11:20.999
